  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1... \nThe surface high holds its sway, with little new to write \ntoday. A multi-day routine of sun and calm; a dry and quiet, \nuneventful balm. The winds are light, the skies are clear. A \nmild and tranquil atmosphere.\n\nBut come late week, there begins a change. For exact scenarios,\nthere is a range. Ensembles diverge by Thursday night, with\nconfidence in any outcome only slight. To our north around then\na shortwave will pass, bringing 30% or less chance of wet \ngrass. A stronger trough by Monday may come about, though exact \ntiming for rain remains in doubt. Onset of moisture shifts later\neach day, keeping the pleasant weather in play. More certainty \nwill come in time, to be sure; for now the finer details remain \nobscure.",
